{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: The peptide was captured from alligator plasma by a custom-built functionalized hydrogel microparticles followed by de novo sequencing by mass spectrometer. Sequence analysis: This is a unique sequence since it shows only 39.3% SIMILARITY TO Latarcin 3b A fragment of blood apolipoprotein C1. Activity: ApoC1(64-88) is active against E. coli (EC50 0.192 uM), P. aeruginosa (EC50 1.41 uM), B. cereus (EC50 0.245 uM), and S. aureus (EC50 9.66 uM). Note that the peptide was not active in Mueller Hinton Broth but could kill bacteria (e.g.. E. coli, S. aureus, P. aeruginosa, and A. baumannii in 10 mM phosphate buffer ( Barksdale et al., 2016). SAR: A further truncated fragment, apoC1(67-88), was also found to be slightly more active against these bacteria. Structure: Peptide (100 ug/ml) is helical in 50% TFE or 60 mM SDS (more helical than A1P, AP2517). Updated Jan2017; 3/2023; 10/2023 based on Monique's email.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "25671663", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2015 Feb 11;10(2):e0117394. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02515", "source_id": "AP02515", "source_numeric_id": "02515", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02515", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Bioprospecting the American Alligator (Alligator mississippiensis) Host Defense Peptidome.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: The peptide was captured from alligator plasma by a custom-built functionalized hydrogel microparticles followed by de nono sequencing by mass spectrometer. It is 36.8% SIMILAR TO Temporin-1Gc Activity: Active against E. coli (EC50 0.332 uM), P. aeruginosa (EC50 7.02 uM), B. cereus (EC50 9.35 uM), and S. aureus (EC50 2.84 uM). SAR: Another further truncated fragment, FGG(401–413), was also identified to be active. Updated 7/2021.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "25671663", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2015 Feb 11;10(2):e0117394. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02516", "source_id": "AP02516", "source_numeric_id": "02516", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02516", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Bioprospecting the American Alligator (Alligator mississippiensis) Host Defense Peptidome.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: The peptide was captured from alligator plasma by a custom-built functionalized hydrogel microparticles followed by de nono sequencing by mass spectrometer. It is 33.3% SIMILAR TO hGAPDH(2-32) Activity: Active against E. coli (EC50 0.0986 uM), P. aeruginosa (EC50 4.35 uM), B. cereus (EC50 0.770 uM), and S. aureus (EC50 1.36 uM). Structure: Helical in 50% TFE (but less helical in SDS). UPdated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "25671663", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2015 Feb 11;10(2):e0117394. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02517", "source_id": "AP02517", "source_numeric_id": "02517", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02517", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Bioprospecting the American Alligator (Alligator mississippiensis) Host Defense Peptidome.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
